schema: test/v2
level: epic
epic: E-EXPORT
branch: epic/export
tests:
  e2e:
    count: 2
    what: "tests/e2e_export.rs — the epic plan's e2e step table walked in order over serve(Config) on ephemeral ports against a local HTTP origin and a local TLS origin: four real exchanges through the proxy (plain GET, POST with a JSON body, decrypted HTTPS, an SSE stream), the listing paged one row at a time and compared against its own order, GET /flows/export parsed as HAR 1.2 with the streamed body carrying size -1 and a streaming comment rather than an empty text, the export filtered and compared, a live /stream subscriber receiving the cleared event naming every removed flow while /stats stays put, the exported bytes re-imported and compared field for field with source flipped and both body endpoints read back, a truncated copy refused 400 with the store unchanged, and a browser-shaped curl command landing as a request-only marked flow followed by one carrying -F refused by name. ui/e2e/specs/capture.spec.ts — the app half through the real Tauri window over the same core: clear behind its ask, a pasted curl command as a marked row, and the ask silenced so the next clear is direct."
  integration:
    count: 1
    what: "every WU landed its own — tests/api.rs covers the four endpoints this epic added or changed (paging envelope and its refusals, export shape and filter, import for both formats and their refusals, clear all/filtered/one and the 404), src/store.rs covers page/import/remove_matching/remove against the ring, and the UI's bounded contract is CaptureControls.test.tsx and CaptureMenu.test.tsx. Counted as one here because the epic adds no integration seam of its own beyond what its WUs asserted; the composition is what the e2e above adds."
  unit:
    count: 1
    what: "603 Rust tests and 840 UI unit tests at this tip, including three properties this epic added: the no-duplicate/no-skip paging invariant over insert/page interleavings, the ring's byte accounting under removals, and toCurl -> parse round-tripping to the same request. The HAR parser is additionally fuzzed with arbitrary bytes for the never-panics claim."
boundary:
  what: "the app-half e2e drives clear (with and without its ask) and the curl paste, not export-to-file or import-from-file"
  why: "in binary mode Tauri defines __TAURI_INTERNALS__.invoke non-writable AND non-configurable and does not consult the wdio Tauri service's mock registry, which is browser-mode only. Assignment, redefinition and replacing the holder were each tried and each refused by the runtime, so the native save and open panels can be neither answered nor passed — pressing export in this harness opens a sheet that never closes. Bending ui/src/ to carry a test-only file seam was rejected: the limit is the harness's. The two file acts are proven over the real engine in tests/e2e_export.rs and against a stubbed native layer in CaptureControls.test.tsx, and the split is recorded as deviation 8 of the epic result."
quirks:
  - quirk: "a body HAR cannot express (streamed, too large, read error) must not read as an empty body"
    test: "tests/e2e_export.rs asserts the SSE entry's content has no text, size -1 and a streaming comment; per-variant unit tests in src/api/har.rs"
  - quirk: "timings phases may not be negative even when the total is HAR's -1"
    test: "har_timings unit tests in src/api/har.rs"
  - quirk: "a clear is not an eviction — a subscriber must be able to tell them apart"
    test: "tests/e2e_export.rs (the cleared event over a live subscriber) and the FlowsCleared/FlowEvicted unit tests in src/api/view.rs"
  - quirk: "a refused import leaves the store exactly as it was"
    test: "tests/e2e_export.rs (a truncated document) and a_refused_import_says_why_and_stores_nothing in tests/api.rs"
  - quirk: "an unsupported curl flag is refused by name rather than ignored"
    test: "tests/e2e_export.rs (-F) and the per-flag unit tests in src/api/curl.rs"
suite:
  rust: "603 tests green (cargo test --all), 0 failed"
  ui_unit: "840 tests green across 49 files (pnpm test)"
  ui_e2e: "31 specs green across three spec files (cargo xtask ui e2e)"
  clippy: "clean under pedantic with --workspace --all-targets, -D warnings"
date: 2026-09-09
